# A MISSING hashed asset must 404 — it must never fall through to index.html.
#
# Why this line exists: with only the SPA rule below, a request for a chunk that
# wasn't at the edge yet (the seconds mid-deploy) returned index.html with HTTP
# 200 and a 4-hour Cache-Control. Browsers cached that HTML *as* the module, so
# every later load failed with "Expected a JavaScript-or-Wasm module script but
# the server responded with a MIME type of text/html" and the whole app died
# behind the error boundary — for hours, surviving ordinary reloads. A 404 is not
# cached as a valid module, so the next load just retries.
/assets/*  /assets/:splat  404

# SPA fallback for real routes.
/* /index.html 200
